# /var/log/pm-sbx/mcp, and root must never open, chown or replace anything inside a folder pm can write. The old config path
# is then only read once, to move an existing config over. When the daemon runs as pm itself (today's start by
# pm-sbx-start-desktop) there is nothing to protect from pm, and the pm-owned folders are the only ones it can write.
